  "body": "**Stacked on #4220** (the multi-axis slice, which is stacked on #4218, the turning slice). The three slices change the same rows of the raw-call guard. Until they merge, this diff also shows their commits (42ca7bfc5, 9886fef31). The commit of this PR is b852d7257. After each parent merges, I merge `main` into this branch.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe 2D and 3D page families of #1122 draw through the form seam.\n\n- **Families.**\n  - 2D (20 files): the 2D milling pages and the cutting pages, with the editors that they share. These are `mill2d_page`, `mill2d_more_page`, `trochoid_page`, `vcarve_page`, `probe_page`, `plasma_page`, `waterjet_page`, `wire_page`, `sinker_page`, `sinker_pick_rows`, `deburr_page`, `pockets_page`, `approach_page`, `predrilled_page`, `rest_pocket_page`, `start_exit_rows`, `pass_start_row`, `load_field`, `lead_page` and `kind_editors`.\n  - 3D: `mill3d_page` and `undercut_page`. They had no raw call on `main`, so this family is one guard row only.\n  - The common operation tabs (`heights_page`, `feeds_page`, `op_page`, `pages`) are not in a family of the #655 list. They stay outside the guard for a later slice.\n- **New seam helpers** (`layout/controls.rs`). Each one is a thin wrapper that draws what the raw call drew:\n  - `button_enabled` and `small_button_enabled`: a greyed-out button;\n  - `checkbox`: a box that is not a property row (the start and exit group headers);\n  - `list_row_truncated`: a list row with an ellipsis (a picked edge);\n  - `note`: a dimmed line that wraps (\"Not taken - ...\");\n  - `drag_row` and `drag_sized_row`: a configured `DragValue` in a `prop_row`, at its own width or at `CTRL_W`. `fields::int_range_row` now draws through `drag_row`.\n- **The raw calls.** About 35 calls in 8 files go through these helpers, or through `list_row`, `button`, `small_button`, `int_range_row` and `text_row`.\n- **Accessible names and the focus ring.** Seven fields now join the pane's Tab / Enter ring (#2516) and have their row's accessible name (#1119): Tab count, Taper angle, Vectors, Turns, EDM condition, Number of passes and Optimal load. Nothing else changes in what the user sees.\n- **The guard** (`layout/form_seam_tests.rs`) gets the 2D and 3D families at 0. It now joins a line that starts with `.` to the line before it, so a call that rustfmt splits after `ui` counts. `deburr_page.rs` had one such call (`ui` / `.add_enabled(`), which the old line count did not see.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/1122-form-seam-2d.md`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `egui_app::layout::form_seam_tests::pages_do_not_add_raw_egui_calls_outside_the_form_seam`: the 2D and 3D families have 0 raw calls.\n- `egui_app::layout::form_seam_tests::form_seam_guard_covers_only_the_migrated_families`: five families, each at 0.\n- `egui_app::layout::form_seam_tests::the_guard_counts_a_raw_call_split_over_two_lines` (new): a split call counts, and a comment line does not.\n- `egui_app::layout::form_seam_tests::the_2d_seam_helpers_keep_clicks_text_and_names` (new):\n  - a greyed-out button and a greyed-out small button take no click;\n  - an enabled button takes one click;\n  - the check box toggles;\n  - the note and the cut list row keep their text;\n  - `drag_row` and `drag_sized_row` fields have their row's name.\n- The page suites that cover the changed rows stay green: `wire_page_tests`, `sinker_machine_tests`, `sinker_pick_rows_tests`, `start_exit_tests`, `turning_start_exit_tests`, `tests::radial_step_field` and `pockets_tests`. All are in the `ui suites: lib` step.\n\nNo new test binary (#3187). The `#[test]` count of `crates/ui` goes up by two.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nThe Wire Contour page, from the off-screen renderer (`egui_kittest` with the headless wgpu device) at 620 x 1400, cropped to the top 540 px.\n- The Passes tab has one skim added, tabs on and the tab count stated. It shows the skim buttons (greyed-out Move up and Move down), Add skim, Tab count and Add tab position.\n- The Geometry tab shows the start and exit group headers and Taper angle.\n\nA pixel comparison of the full frames gives 0 different pixels on both tabs. The images are on the images-only `pr-screenshots` branch of the fork.\n\n| | Before (9886fef31) | After (b852d7257) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Passes | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/1122-2d/before-wire-passes.png) | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/1122-2d/after-wire-passes.png) |\n| Geometry | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/1122-2d/before-wire-geometry.png) | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/1122-2d/after-wire-geometry.png) |\n\n## Gates\n\nOn b852d7257:\n\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`): 10 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (2.5 min). It includes `ui suites: lib` (107 s) and the `boundary`, `sinker_setup` and `waterjet_tool` suites.\n- `cargo clippy --no-deps --all-targets -p camcraft-ui -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Heavy lanes: the diff reaches none.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No check by hand in the GUI window.\n- No screen reader run. The names are checked in the AccessKit tree.\n\nChangelog: Seven operation fields (wire tab count and taper angle, sinker orbit vectors and turns, EDM condition, deburr number of passes, optimal load) join the Tab / Enter field order and have an accessible name.\n\nRefs #1122\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
